        "original_id": "a11035e2-062d-52e6-b597-8590b949d6d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ted Tetzlaff, David Siegel, Scott McGehee, Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, Cleo Moore\n- Works: Gambling House\n- Roles: cinematographer, film director, screenwriter, producer\n- Topics: Hollywood, film noir\n\nFacts:\n- Dale H. \"Ted\" Tetzlaff was born on 3 June 1903 in Los Angeles, California.\n- Ted Tetzlaff was a Hollywood cinematographer active in the 1930s and 1940s.\n- Ted Tetzlaff was nominated for an Academy Award.\n- Gambling House is a 1951 crime film noir directed by Ted Tetzlaff.\n- Gambling House stars Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, and Cleo Moore.\n- David Siegel is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer.\n- David Siegel has a long-standing writing-directing-producing partnership with filmmaker Scott McGehee.\n- Ted Tetzlaff died on 7 January 1995 in Sausalito, California.",
